From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: delete the keys of a freed VLAN group

Upstream fix: hostap main 741d70dd8e32 has the same code; to be
reported upstream.

The AP_VLAN netdev of an AP MLD is shared by its links and stays while
any link has a station on the VLAN. When the last station of the VLAN
leaves one link, for example by a Link Reconfiguration delete, that
link's VLAN group is freed, but its GTK and IGTK stay installed on the
AP_VLAN netdev for the link. A later group of the same VLAN on that link
installs its keys with the same key indexes, and the driver replaces the
stale keys. In mac80211 each replacement waits for an RCU grace period,
so making the group again for a link added by Link Reconfiguration
delayed the Link Reconfiguration Response beyond the 100 ms that a
mac80211 station waits for it.

Delete the group keys of a VLAN group of an MLD authenticator when the
group is freed.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -7131,6 +7131,31 @@ void wpa_auth_pmksa_set_to_sm(struct rsn
 }
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+/* The AP_VLAN netdev of an AP MLD outlives the VLAN group of one link while
+ * other links use it, so the keys of that group go with the group. */
+static void wpa_group_del_vlan_keys(struct wpa_authenticator *wpa_auth,
+				    struct wpa_group *group)
+{
+	int idx;
+
+	if (!wpa_auth->is_ml || group->vlan_id <= 0)
+		return;
+
+	for (idx = 1; idx <= 2; idx++)
+		wpa_auth_set_key(wpa_auth, group->vlan_id, WPA_ALG_NONE, NULL,
+				 idx, NULL, 0, KEY_FLAG_GROUP);
+
+	if (!wpa_auth_pmf_enabled(&wpa_auth->conf))
+		return;
+
+	for (idx = 4; idx <= 5; idx++)
+		wpa_auth_set_key(wpa_auth, group->vlan_id, WPA_ALG_NONE, NULL,
+				 idx, NULL, 0, KEY_FLAG_GROUP);
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
+
 /*
  * Remove and free the group from wpa_authenticator. This is triggered by a
  * callback to make sure nobody is currently iterating the group list while it
@@ -7144,6 +7169,10 @@ static void wpa_group_free(struct wpa_au
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "WPA: Remove group state machine for VLAN-ID %d",
 		   group->vlan_id);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	wpa_group_del_vlan_keys(wpa_auth, group);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	while (prev) {
 		if (prev->next == group) {
 			/* This never frees the special first group as needed */
